{
  "decisions": [
    "2026-09-29, maintainer: the lean set.",
    "Multilingual LibriSpeech is used for anonymous same/different-speaker trials and, by maintainer decision of 2026-09-30, as internal-only Voice Clone references; never speaker identification.",
    "A Zenodo source is pinned by the publisher's MD5 and exact size; its SHA-256 is recorded in the fetch receipt on the first verified fetch and binds every later run.",
    "An unofficial Hugging Face mirror is accepted pinned by revision and LFS SHA-256; its license is cited from the corpus's official source.",
    "2026-10-01, maintainer: QC v2 keeps only the speaker corpora the Voice Clone cell references; the FLEURS train reserve, the accent and the acted-emotion corpora left with QC v1. Japanese and Russian have no acceptable speaker source, so their clone takes use cross-language references."
  ],
  "description": "The pinned speaker corpora whose extractions the take generator's Voice Clone cell draws its reference clips from (cells.clone.referenceSources of config/audio-qc-calibration-takes.json). Only pins, licenses and attributions are committed; the extractions live in the untracked build/cache/audio-qc-corpora, and scripts/qc/corpora.py reads them. The QC v1 fetcher and extractor retired on 2026-10-01; an extraction keeps its identity while its source entry is unchanged.",
  "groups": {
    "speaker": {
      "class": "E",
      "description": "Speaker-labelled read speech: the reference clips of the take generator's Voice Clone cell.",
      "title": "Speaker-labelled speech"
    }
  },
  "hosts": [
    "huggingface.co",
    "*.hf.co",
    "*.huggingface.co",
    "media.githubusercontent.com",
    "raw.githubusercontent.com",
    "zenodo.org"
  ],
  "item": "QC-01",
  "kind": "audio-qc-corpora",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "sources": {
    "aishell3-subset": {
      "alsoIn": [],
      "attribution": "AISHELL-3 (Shi et al., 2021, Interspeech), provided by Beijing Shell Shell Technology Co., Ltd., OpenSLR 93, under the Apache License 2.0; read here from the Hugging Face mirror shenyunhang/AISHELL-3. No audio or transcript is redistributed or committed.",
      "caveats": [
        "An unofficial Hugging Face mirror, pinned by revision and each WAV's LFS SHA-256 (maintainer decision).",
        "A subset of the test split by the seeded rule in subset: 76 speakers with at least 100 utterances, 20 utterances each (about 0.44 GB).",
        "44.1 kHz audio, resampled to 24 kHz; the transcripts interleave characters and pinyin, and text keeps the characters."
      ],
      "extract": {
        "estimateBasis": "the pinned WAV bytes (44.1 kHz PCM16) scaled to 24 kHz",
        "estimatedBytes": 246989789,
        "format": "wav-files",
        "members": "^test/wav/(?P<speaker>SSB[0-9]{4})/(?P<id>SSB[0-9]{8})\\.wav$",
        "metadata": [
          {
            "columns": [
              "speaker",
              "ageGroup",
              "gender",
              "accent"
            ],
            "fields": {
              "accent": "accent",
              "gender": "gender"
            },
            "file": "spk-info.txt",
            "format": "whitespace",
            "joinOn": "speaker",
            "keyColumn": "speaker",
            "optional": true
          },
          {
            "fields": {
              "text": "text"
            },
            "file": "test/content.txt",
            "format": "aishell3-content",
